      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case of a 62-year-old patient presenting with exertional chest pain, atheromatous coronary lesions and left congenital pericardial defect is reported. The diagnostic of peri cardial defect was evoked in relation with a long-known asymptomatic cardiac left malposition and confirmed at surgery. Clinical presentation, diagnosis and management of congenital pericardial defects are discussed."},
